Third-party data bundled with atomipy

The MIT license above covers the atomipy source code. Reference data files
distributed inside the package retain their original licenses and must keep
their accompanying notices:

- atomipy/structures/molecules/ — molecular fragments from the Avogadro2
  project, licensed BSD 3-Clause (Copyright (c) 2016 Geoffrey Hutchison,
  University of Pittsburgh). See atomipy/structures/molecules/LICENSE.
- atomipy/structures/ (minerals, crystals, …) — crystallographic structures
  derived from open databases (e.g. COD / AMCSD); their original terms and
  attribution apply.
- atomipy/ffparams/min.ff/ — the MINFF force field (github.com/mholmboe/minff)
  and CLAYFF parameters are compiled from the published literature; cite the
  original papers referenced in the force-field files when using them.
